>> title: Salsa Verde
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: tomatillo, chiles, mexican, vegetarian, stovetop
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: verde, salsa verde asada, green salsa, salsa de tomatillo, table salsa, salsa verde cocida
>> pairs-with: salsa-roja, corn-tortillas
>> servings: 6
>> time: 30 min
>> step.1: char 10 min
>> step.2: blend coarse
>> step.3: fry 5 min
>> step.4: finish off heat

Char @tomatillos{1%lb}(450 g; husked and rinsed), @white onion{1/2%medium}(thick slices), @garlic{3%cloves}(unpeeled; peel after charring), and @serrano chiles{3} on a dry #comal{} for ~toast{10%min}, turning until they slump and blacken in patches.

Blend @&(~1)charred vegetables{} with @cilantro{1/4%cup}(leaves and stems) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} to a coarse purée.

Fry @&(~1)salsa{} in @vegetable oil{1%Tbs} over high heat for ~fry{5%min}, until it darkens from bright green to olive and pulls together.

Finish @&(~1)salsa{} off the heat with @fresh lime juice{1%tsp} and @white onion{2%Tbs}(finely chopped).
